[{:db/id 17592186161923 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8899331b-91a4-5c31-88b7-72adb8fd73b2" "question-cdd1fbde-a478-5539-a14c-9c15409e9daa"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161732 :question/problem "Given that ![](images/73/735c42b1482105bf9f070dee3f615bdca83ab9e4559b8ae005f28b7726227c5d.svg) calculate ![](images/1b/1bb0a52154bb23ae44fa926a0b9850f177ede8308ede6e0c9d371f3c3686abb8.svg) Round your final answer to four decimal places.\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n![](images/d7/d71af572591794e164e753e941f4acd94d6c06b4a57d2dd6fd9f0936665b80b9.svg)\n\n*The probability density function ![](images/93/93f888a1ee0b7da5e29f442f803f1c0eaf73ad02f5eaa97e85bb8a35d607015b.svg) is given by*\n\n![](images/56/564fc9ff1a6f01c56f27eee8db922e81dfc26f6861c8c36693882babe5d23af5.svg)" :question/worked-solution "A chi-square random variable ![](images/db/db399a1c841bf0249a3613b23cdadcb5b98da7ae33373aeecc1a1d3bf375a848.svg) with ![](images/8d/8dc6f7e80ecaac9fa07890ce1881dd51de319597ae8b1dce821aa03c1f3eff06.svg) degrees of freedom has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/d6/d6866528a5e752d3ace0c352dbdd41efc7e3d164aa19e19d7ec0cee353039ba2.svg)\n\nWe're given that ![](images/e1/e1ff0a26da8639429e843436fe938b5a08f1ff1c0004181a536341bae8849ff5.svg) So, ![](images/46/46833dd7644e5c60bb4525fe4e7649a99752b26096331755a4b44c2abe183f11.svg) has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/5e/5e86fa058cb30fe31938e66e60f5fc9f6c8c143f97b33efb430dc6cad2ef7580.svg)\n\nRecalling that ![](images/7f/7fa47747cfccdd9e248ce57cf47677d0442a3cecb12c5a87fd2047666449bdd3.svg) for any natural number ![](images/05/053c53695c9135de14fbf7f1107641b09bc58e3f64ab77189037b79f6202aeff.svg) we have\n\n![](images/9a/9a61c71b697579d90b9a0bb90cd2a2ba252e74acd40b139b3cf85f9284609ca3.svg)\n\nSo, the probability distribution becomes\n\n![](images/9a/9a6f0b77892fb76598596992be35903b302ce14191b448a1adcce1f518b3612a.svg)\n\nFinally, we calculate ![](images/81/81b8764208b2f6a31a51bf2f27f709db42357e4c09c83e33432dd205b2c172aa.svg) as follows:\n\n![](images/e9/e9e12db3d55238bb5b33f68a325ede84caa1c37d4cd97f3e4eee3c75975d8796.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161924 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4082c7b9-656c-5af0-a7d3-4e13cbac6782"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161733 :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\geq x) = p,$ where $X\\sim \\chi^2(k).$ Given that the random variable $X \\sim \\chi^2(7),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X \\geq x) = 0.99.$\n\n| $k \\setminus p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $\\,0.412\\,$ | $\\,0.554\\,$ | $\\,0.831\\,$ | $\\,1.145\\,$ | $\\,1.610\\,$ |\n| $6$ | $\\,0.676\\,$ | $\\,0.872\\,$ | $\\,1.237\\,$ | $\\,1.635\\,$ | $\\,2.204\\,$ |\n| $7$ | $\\,0.989\\,$ | $\\,1.239\\,$ | $\\,1.690\\,$ | $\\,2.167\\,$ | $\\,2.833\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Since $X \\sim \\chi^2(7),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=7.$\n\n| $k \\setminus p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $7$ | $\\,0.989\\,$ | $\\,1.239\\,$ | $\\,1.690\\,$ | $\\,2.167\\,$ | $\\,2.833\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X \\geq 1.239) = 0.990.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=1.239.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161925 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-824977e3-712a-57cf-beb4-b57ff8f0ad52"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161734 :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\geq x) = p,$ where $X\\sim \\chi^2(k).$ Given that $X \\sim \\chi^2(7),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X \\leq x) = 0.005.$\n\n| $k \\setminus p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $\\,0.412\\,$ | $\\,0.554\\,$ | $\\,0.831\\,$ | $\\,1.145\\,$ | $\\,1.610\\,$ |\n| $6$ | $\\,0.676\\,$ | $\\,0.872\\,$ | $\\,1.237\\,$ | $\\,1.635\\,$ | $\\,2.204\\,$ |\n| $7$ | $\\,0.989\\,$ | $\\,1.239\\,$ | $\\,1.690\\,$ | $\\,2.167\\,$ | $\\,2.833\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The table shows probabilities in the form $P(X > x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>x) & =1-P(X\\le x) \\\\  & =1-0.005 \\\\  & =0.995\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $X \\sim \\chi^2(7),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=7.$\n\n| $k \\setminus p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $7$ | $\\,0.989\\,$ | $\\,1.239\\,$ | $\\,1.690\\,$ | $\\,2.167\\,$ | $\\,2.833\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X > 0.989) = 0.995.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=0.989.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161926 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-133afd92-ce15-5e18-bd34-c90446f47667" "question-6afc0dfa-f42f-5b87-9c8b-8fbf362ef997"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161735 :question/problem "Let the random variable $Y$ be defined as\n\n$$\nY = Z_1^2+Z_2^2+\\cdots + Z_{10}^2\n$$\n\nwhere $Z_i\\sim N(0,1)$ for $1\\leq i\\leq 10.$ Find the value $y$ that satisfies $P(Y\\leq y) = 0.99.$\n\n*Hint: The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\geq x) = p,$ where $X\\sim \\chi^2(k).$*\n\n| $k \\setminus p$ | $0.010$ | $0.050$ | $0.100$ | $0.150$ | $0.200$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $8$ | $\\,20.090\\,$ | $\\,15.507\\,$ | $\\,13.362\\,$ | $\\,12.027\\,$ | $\\,11.030\\,$ |\n| $9$ | $\\,21.666\\,$ | $\\,16.919\\,$ | $\\,14.684\\,$ | $\\,13.288\\,$ | $\\,12.242\\,$ |\n| $10$ | $\\,23.209\\,$ | $\\,18.307\\,$ | $\\,15.987\\,$ | $\\,14.534\\,$ | $\\,13.442\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "If $Z_i\\sim N(0,1)$ for $1\\leq i \\leq k$ are independent normal random variables, then the sum\n\n$$\nZ_1^2+Z_2^2+\\cdots + Z_{k}^2\n$$\n\nfollows a $\\chi^2(k)$ distribution with $k$ degrees of freedom.\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\nY = Z_1^2+Z_2^2+\\cdots + Z_{10}^2 \\sim \\chi^2(10).\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the given probability in the form $P(Y\\geq y){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le y) & =1-P(Y\\ge y) \\\\ 0.99 & =1-P(Y\\ge y) \\\\ P(Y\\ge y) & =0.01\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we wish to find the value $y$ such that $P(Y\\geq y) = 0.01$ This can be found from the given table:\n\n| $k \\setminus p$ | $0.010$ | $0.050$ | $0.100$ | $0.150$ | $0.200$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $8$ | $\\,20.090\\,$ | $\\,15.507\\,$ | $\\,13.362\\,$ | $\\,12.027\\,$ | $\\,11.030\\,$ |\n| $9$ | $\\,21.666\\,$ | $\\,16.919\\,$ | $\\,14.684\\,$ | $\\,13.288\\,$ | $\\,12.242\\,$ |\n| $10$ | $\\,\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}23.209}\\,$ | $\\,18.307\\,$ | $\\,15.987\\,$ | $\\,14.534\\,$ | $\\,13.442\\,$ |\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y\\geq 23.209) = 0.01\n$$\n\nwhich means\n\n$$\nP(Y\\leq 23.209) = 0.99.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value $y$ that satisfies $P(Y\\leq y) = 0.99$ is $y=\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}23.209}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-8899331b-91a4-5c31-88b7-72adb8fd73b2" :question/id #uuid "8899331b-91a4-5c31-88b7-72adb8fd73b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-108162" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼{χ}^{2}(8),$ calculate $P(X<6).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places.\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{6}{x}^{3}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x≈33.86574\n$$\n\n*The probability density function ${χ}^{2}(k)$ is given by*\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{2}^{k/2}Γ(\\frac{k}{2})}{x}^{k/2-1}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A chi-square random variable $X∼{χ}^{2}(k)$ with $k$ degrees of freedom has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{2}^{k/2}Γ(\\frac{k}{2})}{x}^{k/2-1}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $X∼{χ}^{2}(8).$ So, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{16Γ(4)}{x}^{3}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecalling that $Γ(n)=(n-1)!$ for any natural number $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\nΓ(4)=3!=6.\n$$\n\nSo, the probability distribution becomes\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{96}{x}^{3}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate $P(X<6)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<6) & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{96}{x}^{3}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{96}{\\int }_{0}^{6}{x}^{3}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ≈\\frac{1}{96}\\cdot 33.86574 \\\\  & ≈0.3528\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4d46e94c-f4ab-56b9-8e85-c4389bca8a23"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4d46e94c-f4ab-56b9-8e85-c4389bca8a23" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d46e94c-f4ab-56b9-8e85-c4389bca8a23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cf6d6f91-79a7-500f-bfdc-0476ab995d9d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2454fa59-6173-5a32-9c1b-31dc5e951511" "answer-cf6d6f91-79a7-500f-bfdc-0476ab995d9d" "answer-0823d426-5b2c-5ac6-b64a-d3179098eb29" "answer-5dcf242e-be31-5257-85a8-128cc12f3f68" "answer-71f6e868-dd1f-5adf-83d1-cf86121aa303"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2454fa59-6173-5a32-9c1b-31dc5e951511" :answer/id #uuid "2454fa59-6173-5a32-9c1b-31dc5e951511" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3253" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf6d6f91-79a7-500f-bfdc-0476ab995d9d" :answer/id #uuid "cf6d6f91-79a7-500f-bfdc-0476ab995d9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3528" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0823d426-5b2c-5ac6-b64a-d3179098eb29" :answer/id #uuid "0823d426-5b2c-5ac6-b64a-d3179098eb29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8528" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5dcf242e-be31-5257-85a8-128cc12f3f68" :answer/id #uuid "5dcf242e-be31-5257-85a8-128cc12f3f68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.3288" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71f6e868-dd1f-5adf-83d1-cf86121aa303" :answer/id #uuid "71f6e868-dd1f-5adf-83d1-cf86121aa303" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.8528" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cdd1fbde-a478-5539-a14c-9c15409e9daa" :question/id #uuid "cdd1fbde-a478-5539-a14c-9c15409e9daa" :question/math-academy-id "q-108186" :question/problem "Given that $X∼{χ}^{2}(8),$ what is $P(X<6)$ expressed as an integral?\n\n*Hint: The probability density function ${χ}^{2}(k)$ is given by*\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{2}^{k/2}Γ(\\frac{k}{2})}{x}^{k/2-1}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A chi-square random variable $X∼{χ}^{2}(k)$ with $k$ degrees of freedom has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{2}^{k/2}Γ(\\frac{k}{2})}{x}^{k/2-1}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $X∼{χ}^{2}(8).$ So, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{16Γ(4)}{x}^{3}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecalling that $Γ(n)=(n-1)!$ for any natural number $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\nΓ(4)=3!=6.\n$$\n\nSo, the probability distribution becomes\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{96}{x}^{3}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate $P(X<6)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<6) & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{96}{x}^{3}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{96}{\\int }_{0}^{6}{x}^{3}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8ee5e6c9-fa4a-58fc-ae2e-8a2fef0c2570"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8ee5e6c9-fa4a-58fc-ae2e-8a2fef0c2570" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ee5e6c9-fa4a-58fc-ae2e-8a2fef0c2570" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-96eba1c0-859c-5458-a39c-079d9f2b36ac" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5c72f2e6-f2e4-5cc9-b22d-6cda68c3cf7f" "answer-591bfd80-a947-5044-b7df-6ae75531398e" "answer-dce09a64-208d-5c8a-9fbb-34460d664adf" "answer-96eba1c0-859c-5458-a39c-079d9f2b36ac" "answer-2efa2847-8c8c-50f1-b144-1c847e19fa35"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c72f2e6-f2e4-5cc9-b22d-6cda68c3cf7f" :answer/id #uuid "5c72f2e6-f2e4-5cc9-b22d-6cda68c3cf7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{6}{x}^{3}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-591bfd80-a947-5044-b7df-6ae75531398e" :answer/id #uuid "591bfd80-a947-5044-b7df-6ae75531398e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{6}{x}^{4}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dce09a64-208d-5c8a-9fbb-34460d664adf" :answer/id #uuid "dce09a64-208d-5c8a-9fbb-34460d664adf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{6}{x}^{2}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96eba1c0-859c-5458-a39c-079d9f2b36ac" :answer/id #uuid "96eba1c0-859c-5458-a39c-079d9f2b36ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{96}{\\int }_{0}^{6}{x}^{3}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2efa2847-8c8c-50f1-b144-1c847e19fa35" :answer/id #uuid "2efa2847-8c8c-50f1-b144-1c847e19fa35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{96}{\\int }_{0}^{6}{x}^{6}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162238 :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$  Given that the random variable $X∼{χ}^{2}(5),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X\\ge x)=0.99.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $\\,0.072\\,$ | $\\,0.115\\,$ | $\\,0.216\\,$ | $\\,0.352\\,$ | $\\,0.584\\,$ |\n| $4$ | $\\,0.207\\,$ | $\\,0.297\\,$ | $\\,0.484\\,$ | $\\,0.711\\,$ | $\\,1.064\\,$ |\n| $5$ | $\\,0.412\\,$ | $\\,0.554\\,$ | $\\,0.831\\,$ | $\\,1.145\\,$ | $\\,1.610\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Since $X∼{χ}^{2}(5),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=5.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $\\,0.412\\,$ | $\\,0.554\\,$ | $\\,0.831\\,$ | $\\,1.145\\,$ | $\\,1.610\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 0.554)=0.99.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=0.554.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186158630 :answer-field/correct 17592186158633 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-4082c7b9-656c-5af0-a7d3-4e13cbac6782" :question/id #uuid "4082c7b9-656c-5af0-a7d3-4e13cbac6782" :question/math-academy-id "q-108266" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$  Given that the random variable $X∼{χ}^{2}(8),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X>x)=0.950.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $6$ | $\\,0.676\\,$ | $\\,0.872\\,$ | $\\,1.237\\,$ | $\\,1.635\\,$ | $\\,2.204\\,$ |\n| $7$ | $\\,0.989\\,$ | $\\,1.239\\,$ | $\\,1.690\\,$ | $\\,2.167\\,$ | $\\,2.833\\,$ |\n| $8$ | $\\,1.344\\,$ | $\\,1.646\\,$ | $\\,2.180\\,$ | $\\,2.733\\,$ | $\\,3.490\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Since $X∼{χ}^{2}(8),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=8.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $8$ | $\\,1.344\\,$ | $\\,1.646\\,$ | $\\,2.180\\,$ | $\\,2.733\\,$ | $\\,3.490\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X>2.733)=0.950.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=2.733.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3542c59a-a8e5-5ff3-a238-b0c908d6f40c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3542c59a-a8e5-5ff3-a238-b0c908d6f40c" :answer-field/id #uuid "3542c59a-a8e5-5ff3-a238-b0c908d6f40c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-78259eea-9d16-59de-adab-2a8608c1fee3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-37aa76aa-7b11-559a-bc29-93953852d106" "answer-92d4a73f-849b-57cb-8c77-3eb3d9c58a2e" "answer-4a171e19-08b7-5dfb-88ec-745eba58dd09" "answer-78259eea-9d16-59de-adab-2a8608c1fee3" "answer-9060b685-b5b9-5d63-9a14-913d1e947150"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37aa76aa-7b11-559a-bc29-93953852d106" :answer/id #uuid "37aa76aa-7b11-559a-bc29-93953852d106" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.676" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92d4a73f-849b-57cb-8c77-3eb3d9c58a2e" :answer/id #uuid "92d4a73f-849b-57cb-8c77-3eb3d9c58a2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.646" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a171e19-08b7-5dfb-88ec-745eba58dd09" :answer/id #uuid "4a171e19-08b7-5dfb-88ec-745eba58dd09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.204" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78259eea-9d16-59de-adab-2a8608c1fee3" :answer/id #uuid "78259eea-9d16-59de-adab-2a8608c1fee3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.733" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9060b685-b5b9-5d63-9a14-913d1e947150" :answer/id #uuid "9060b685-b5b9-5d63-9a14-913d1e947150" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.490" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-824977e3-712a-57cf-beb4-b57ff8f0ad52" :question/id #uuid "824977e3-712a-57cf-beb4-b57ff8f0ad52" :question/math-academy-id "q-108300" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$ Given that $X∼{χ}^{2}(4),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X\\le x)=0.025.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $\\,0.072\\,$ | $\\,0.115\\,$ | $\\,0.216\\,$ | $\\,0.352\\,$ | $\\,0.584\\,$ |\n| $4$ | $\\,0.207\\,$ | $\\,0.297\\,$ | $\\,0.484\\,$ | $\\,0.711\\,$ | $\\,1.064\\,$ |\n| $5$ | $\\,0.412\\,$ | $\\,0.554\\,$ | $\\,0.831\\,$ | $\\,1.145\\,$ | $\\,1.610\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The table shows probabilities in the form $P(X>x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>x) & =1-P(X\\le x) \\\\  & =1-0.025 \\\\  & =0.975\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{χ}^{2}(4),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=4.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $\\,0.207\\,$ | $\\,0.297\\,$ | $\\,0.484\\,$ | $\\,0.711\\,$ | $\\,1.064\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X>0.484)=0.975.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=0.484.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2b906fde-e2cb-5d14-8bd5-4b7e10aeffe7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2b906fde-e2cb-5d14-8bd5-4b7e10aeffe7" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b906fde-e2cb-5d14-8bd5-4b7e10aeffe7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0fb991ce-4b7c-5de9-ab03-280608b86db1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-82a0784c-9e11-58e5-9dbf-fe2eada81cae" "answer-cb2e1dff-1f23-5716-942e-08efd9188695" "answer-0fb991ce-4b7c-5de9-ab03-280608b86db1" "answer-36a9fc04-92a0-545c-a9b1-c789f48da005" "answer-29c35df3-8e92-5fc7-a88c-ae44748bd3b0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82a0784c-9e11-58e5-9dbf-fe2eada81cae" :answer/id #uuid "82a0784c-9e11-58e5-9dbf-fe2eada81cae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.404" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb2e1dff-1f23-5716-942e-08efd9188695" :answer/id #uuid "cb2e1dff-1f23-5716-942e-08efd9188695" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.443" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0fb991ce-4b7c-5de9-ab03-280608b86db1" :answer/id #uuid "0fb991ce-4b7c-5de9-ab03-280608b86db1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.484" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36a9fc04-92a0-545c-a9b1-c789f48da005" :answer/id #uuid "36a9fc04-92a0-545c-a9b1-c789f48da005" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.084" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29c35df3-8e92-5fc7-a88c-ae44748bd3b0" :answer/id #uuid "29c35df3-8e92-5fc7-a88c-ae44748bd3b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.344" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162241 :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$ Given that $X∼{χ}^{2}(9),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X\\le x)=0.05.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $7$ | $\\,0.989\\,$ | $\\,1.239\\,$ | $\\,1.690\\,$ | $\\,2.167\\,$ | $\\,2.833\\,$ |\n| $8$ | $\\,1.344\\,$ | $\\,1.646\\,$ | $\\,2.180\\,$ | $\\,2.733\\,$ | $\\,3.490\\,$ |\n| $9$ | $\\,1.735\\,$ | $\\,2.088\\,$ | $\\,2.700\\,$ | $\\,3.325\\,$ | $\\,4.168\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The table shows probabilities in the form $P(X>x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>x) & =1-P(X\\le x) \\\\  & =1-0.05 \\\\  & =0.95\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{χ}^{2}(9),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=9.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $9$ | $\\,1.735\\,$ | $\\,2.088\\,$ | $\\,2.700\\,$ | $\\,3.325\\,$ | $\\,4.168\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X>3.325)=0.950.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=3.325.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186158648 :answer-field/correct 17592186158651 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-133afd92-ce15-5e18-bd34-c90446f47667" :question/id #uuid "133afd92-ce15-5e18-bd34-c90446f47667" :question/math-academy-id "q-252035" :question/problem "Let the random variable $Y$ be defined as\n\n$$\nY={Z}_{1}^{2}+{Z}_{2}^{2}+⋯+{Z}_{25}^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${Z}_{i}∼N(0,1)$ for $1\\le i\\le 25.$ Find the value $y$ such that $P(Y\\ge y)=0.1.$\n\n*Hint: The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.010$ | $0.050$ | $0.100$ | $0.150$ | $0.200$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $25$ | $\\,44.314\\,$ | $\\,37.652\\,$ | $\\,34.382\\,$ | $\\,32.282\\,$ | $\\,30.675\\,$ |\n| $26$ | $\\,45.642\\,$ | $\\,38.885\\,$ | $\\,35.563\\,$ | $\\,33.429\\,$ | $\\,31.795\\,$ |\n| $27$ | $\\,46.963\\,$ | $\\,40.113\\,$ | $\\,36.741\\,$ | $\\,34.574\\,$ | $\\,32.912\\,$ |\n\nThe value of $y$ that satisfies $P(Y\\ge y)=0.1$ is $y=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "If ${Z}_{i}∼N(0,1)$ for $1\\le i\\le k$ are independent normal random variables, then the sum\n\n$$\n{Z}_{1}^{2}+{Z}_{2}^{2}+⋯+{Z}_{k}^{2}\n$$\n\nfollows a ${χ}^{2}(k)$ distribution with $k$ degrees of freedom.\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\nY={Z}_{1}^{2}+{Z}_{2}^{2}+⋯+{Z}_{25}^{2}∼{χ}^{2}(25).\n$$\n\nWe wish to find the value $y$ such that $P(Y\\ge y)=0.1$ This can be found from the given table:\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.010$ | $0.050$ | $0.100$ | $0.150$ | $0.200$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $25$ | $\\,44.314\\,$ | $\\,37.652\\,$ | $\\,34.382\\,$ | $\\,32.282\\,$ | $\\,30.675\\,$ |\n| $26$ | $\\,45.642\\,$ | $\\,38.885\\,$ | $\\,35.563\\,$ | $\\,33.429\\,$ | $\\,31.795\\,$ |\n| $27$ | $\\,46.963\\,$ | $\\,40.113\\,$ | $\\,36.741\\,$ | $\\,34.574\\,$ | $\\,32.912\\,$ |\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y\\ge 34.382)=0.1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=34.382.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-649de251-3200-5093-ae42-9bf3c6fa21ab"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-649de251-3200-5093-ae42-9bf3c6fa21ab" :answer-field/id #uuid "649de251-3200-5093-ae42-9bf3c6fa21ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c2fdfce5-219e-5618-a11d-545dab309523" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c2fdfce5-219e-5618-a11d-545dab309523"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2fdfce5-219e-5618-a11d-545dab309523" :answer/id #uuid "c2fdfce5-219e-5618-a11d-545dab309523" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "34.382" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6afc0dfa-f42f-5b87-9c8b-8fbf362ef997" :question/id #uuid "6afc0dfa-f42f-5b87-9c8b-8fbf362ef997" :question/math-academy-id "q-252038" :question/problem "Let the random variable $Y$ be defined as\n\n$$\nY={Z}_{1}^{2}+{Z}_{2}^{2}+⋯+{Z}_{40}^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${Z}_{i}∼N(0,1)$ for $1\\le i\\le 40.$ Find the value $y$ such that $P(Y\\ge y)=0.15.$\n\n*Hint: The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.010$ | $0.050$ | $0.100$ | $0.150$ | $0.200$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $39$ | $\\,62.428\\,$ | $\\,54.572\\,$ | $\\,50.660\\,$ | $\\,48.126\\,$ | $\\,46.173\\,$ |\n| $40$ | $\\,63.691\\,$ | $\\,55.758\\,$ | $\\,51.805\\,$ | $\\,49.244\\,$ | $\\,47.269\\,$ |\n| $41$ | $\\,64.950\\,$ | $\\,56.942\\,$ | $\\,52.949\\,$ | $\\,50.360\\,$ | $\\,48.363\\,$ |\n\nThe value of $y$ that satisfies $P(Y\\ge y)=0.15$ is $y=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "If ${Z}_{i}∼N(0,1)$ for $1\\le i\\le k$ are independent normal random variables, then the sum\n\n$$\n{Z}_{1}^{2}+{Z}_{2}^{2}+⋯+{Z}_{k}^{2}\n$$\n\nfollows a ${χ}^{2}(k)$ distribution with $k$ degrees of freedom.\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\nY={Z}_{1}^{2}+{Z}_{2}^{2}+⋯+{Z}_{40}^{2}∼{χ}^{2}(40).\n$$\n\nWe wish to find the value $y$ such that $P(Y\\ge y)=0.15$ This can be found from the given table:\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.010$ | $0.050$ | $0.100$ | $0.150$ | $0.200$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $39$ | $\\,62.428\\,$ | $\\,54.572\\,$ | $\\,50.660\\,$ | $\\,48.126\\,$ | $\\,46.173\\,$ |\n| $40$ | $\\,63.691\\,$ | $\\,55.758\\,$ | $\\,51.805\\,$ | $\\,49.244\\,$ | $\\,47.269\\,$ |\n| $41$ | $\\,64.950\\,$ | $\\,56.942\\,$ | $\\,52.949\\,$ | $\\,50.360\\,$ | $\\,48.363\\,$ |\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y\\ge 49.244)=0.15.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=49.244.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f463de34-0bb9-5c30-8c20-f9ac90effe8f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f463de34-0bb9-5c30-8c20-f9ac90effe8f" :answer-field/id #uuid "f463de34-0bb9-5c30-8c20-f9ac90effe8f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-603c5297-e6ee-5028-b2ef-27ebcb3c175c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-603c5297-e6ee-5028-b2ef-27ebcb3c175c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-603c5297-e6ee-5028-b2ef-27ebcb3c175c" :answer/id #uuid "603c5297-e6ee-5028-b2ef-27ebcb3c175c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "49.244" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163177 :tutorial/content "**The chi-square distribution** with $k$ **degrees of freedom**, denoted $\\chi^2(k)$, is the distribution of a random variable that is the sum of the squares of $k$ independent standard normal random variables. \n\nThus, if $Z_1, Z_2, \\ldots, Z_k$ are mutually independent, where $Z_i\\sim N(0,1)$, then\n\n$$\nZ_1^2+Z_2^2+\\ldots+Z_k^2\\sim  \\chi^2(k).\n$$\n\nIt can be shown that $X \\sim \\chi^2(k)$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/6a/6a46942ee5d42c721fb23905e49a67d28c2916eecc234e86734263c599df49fc.svg)\n\nNote that $\\Gamma$ is the gamma function.\n\nThe diagram below shows $f(x)$ for various degrees of freedom $k.$\n\n![](images/ce/cecc3fc82e618f5b5f91e61c4dcab6c1d38b970af20f0ae2baf929b0ce9cdbb3.png)\n\nThe chi-square distribution is widely used in inferential statistics. In particular, it is used in **goodness of fit** tests, where experimental data is compared against a hypothesized theoretical model. You will learn more about the applications of the chi-square distribution in future lessons." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163178 :tutorial/content "Let $X\\sim\\chi^2(3).$ Suppose we wish to know the specific value $x$ such that \n\n$$\nP(X\\geq x) = 0.05.\n$$\n\nHere, $\\alpha = 0.05$ is sometimes called the **significance level**. The required probability is represented by the shaded region below.\n\n![](images/34/34551dd57f17cfb0bdd3bebd2d09c907615f3d936e4b5d69083517d17c1f779f.png)\n\nWe often resort to percentage points tables to look up our desired values rather than computing these probabilities by hand (which would be very difficult). \n\nSome percentage points for the $\\chi^2(3)$ distribution are given below. Each cell in the table gives a value $x$ such that $P(X\\geq x) = p$ for a particular value of $p.$\n\n| $k \\setminus p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $\\,6.251\\,$ | $\\,7.815\\,$ | $\\,9.348\\,$ | $\\,11.345\\,$ | $\\,12.838\\,$ |\n\nFrom the table, we have\n\n$$\nP(X \\geq 7.815) = 0.05.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x = 7.815.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162177 :activity/expected-seconds 600.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
